fe.append_section(S, '02', '## Seeing the impossible date roll over', """Run this in Node before you trust `realDate`:

```js
> new Date("2027-02-29T00:00:00Z").toISOString()
'2027-03-01T00:00:00.000Z'
> new Date("2028-02-29T00:00:00Z").toISOString()
'2028-02-29T00:00:00.000Z'
```

`Date.parse` does not reject an impossible day; it rolls it into the next month. That is why `realDate` in `server/server.js` re-serializes the parsed instant and compares the first ten characters with the input: only a date that survives the round trip is real. A validator that checks the regex alone would accept `2027-02-29` and store March 1.""")
